+# Panel languages (English / Chinese) Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Implement the panel-i18n design (spec revision 2, human-approved, H18) exactly: every piece of text the Orca web panel shows can be read in English or Chinese through react-i18next; the language follows the browser by default and a manual choice is remembered in that browser (`orca.panel.lang`); English stays byte-identical to today's panel; the loop-plan view sends fields instead of English sentences; metrics and coverage sentences gain stable codes; refusals show a Chinese text by code with the server's message as the visible fallback.
+
+**Architecture:** One i18next instance of the panel's own (`createInstance()` in `web/src/i18n.ts`), initialised synchronously from two statically imported resources, `web/src/locales/en.ts` (the source shape, `as const`, byte-identical to today's text) and `web/src/locales/zh.ts` (typed `Translation<typeof en>`, so a missing or extra key is a compile error), plus a Chinese-only `zhErrors` table keyed by refusal code. Components call `useTranslation()`; helpers keep their signatures and translate through the shared instance at call time (every helper is called during the render of a component that uses `useTranslation`, so a language change reaches them). Enum values rendered raw go through `enumText(family, value)`, whose English families are `Record`s over the value unions (a new value is a compile error) and which shows an unknown value as sent. The server's loop-plan view drops `planName`/`summary` and adds `maxFiles`/`hasDiscipline`; the panel builds the lines with `t`, the registry in `src/control/loopPlans.ts` stays the English source of record and a criterion pins the English resource to it. A committed TypeScript-parse scan (`scripts/scan-panel-text.mjs`) lists every text site in `web/src`; the last task pins that nothing but a named allow-list is left, and a pseudo-locale render of every area pins that everything visible goes through `t`.
+
+**Tech Stack:** TypeScript (NodeNext root, Bundler web), React 19, i18next `^26.4.2`, react-i18next `^17.0.15`, i18next-browser-languagedetector `^8.2.1`, vitest 2 (+ jsdom, @testing-library/react), zod 3 on the server.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-01-panel-i18n-design.md` (revision 2; §9 lists its review; approved by the human, ledger H18: "spec 同意，§6.1 的判据改写都授权，写计划吧"). Rulings L1–L6 are not reopened here.
+
+> Drafter: read-only drafting sub-agent of Orca session `e604b1ba` (Claude Opus 5.5), 2026-10-01. Nothing in the repository but this file was written; probes (a scratch install of the three libraries, the scan, the `describeLoopPlan` capture) ran in the session scratchpad `…/scratchpad/i18nplan/`.
+> Observation anchor: Orca subject `fix(web): applying a suggestion keeps the plan card's open draft` (`ac969bb`). Line numbers are "measured 2026-10-01 at that commit, re-measure before use" (Rule 14); each Task's executor re-measures after the previous Task's commit.
